            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No problem! Sorry, didn't recognize you as the author of 'nvim-various-textobjs'. Nice job!\n\nI always wondered if you get user issues that come from default keymaps. There are several that don't start with `i` or `a` which can cause problems with some operators (especially if they have \"single line\" variant like `grr`). For example, the \"restOfParagraph\" textobject with its default `r` mapping won't properly work with `gr` if there is `grr` mapping.",
