            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> No problem! Sorry, didn't recognize you as the author of 'nvim-various-textobjs'. Nice job!\n\nAll good, it's rather small in comparison to mini.nvim anyway. Thank you, praise from such a prolific dev as you means a lot!\n\n> I always wondered if you get user issues that come from default keymaps. There are several that don't start with i or a which can cause problems with some operators (especially if they have \"single line\" variant like grr). For example, the \"restOfParagraph\" textobject with its default r mapping won't properly work with gr if there is grr mapping.\n\nActually, not so much. With so many text objects, there potential conflicts are pretty much unavoidable. However, [the defaults need explicitly opted in to, and you can also opt out of selected defaults mappings](https://github.com/chrisgrieser/nvim-various-textobjs?tab=readme-ov-file#options), thus the mappings aren't that much trouble. \n\nI occasionally get comparisons/references to `mini.ai` though. Like, for instance, recently I had an issue with \"your quote object ignores escaped quotes, while the mini-ai object only considers balanced quotes. Could this plugin support balanced, unescaped quotes?\"\n(Just in case you wanna in turn take that one from me: [I repurposed frontier patterns as mini-lookbehinds to exclude escaped quotes.](https://github.com/chrisgrieser/nvim-various-textobjs/blob/dd6d862dd9a782f96eec21a26dfbebbbc79b7d4d/lua/various-textobjs/textobjs/charwise.lua#L33-L59))",
