        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> (Just in case you wanna in turn take that one from me: [I repurposed frontier patterns as mini-lookbehinds to exclude escaped quotes.](https://github.com/chrisgrieser/nvim-various-textobjs/blob/dd6d862dd9a782f96eec21a26dfbebbbc79b7d4d/lua/various-textobjs/textobjs/charwise.lua#L33-L59))\n\nThat's nice, but a bit magical for my taste. Escaped quotes shouldn't be too frequent occurrence which can be adjusted manually.\n\nAnd also be careful with using frontier patterns. They are only LuaJIT and Lua 5.2+ compatible. Neovim plugins ideally should only use Lua 5.1 features (as stated in `:h lua-compat`) and frontier pattern is not. That said, they are useful and 'mini.nvim' uses them in several places (because I didn't know about the compatibility during writing 'mini.ai' and friends).",
