        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> That's nice, but a bit magical for my taste. Escaped quotes shouldn't be too frequent occurrence which can be adjusted manually.\n\nDepends a bit on the situation. In some filetypes, they are unavoidable (json) or at least much more frequent (shell scripts).\n\n> And also be careful with using frontier patterns. They are only LuaJIT and Lua 5.2+ compatible. Neovim plugins ideally should only use Lua 5.1 features (as stated in :h lua-compat) and frontier pattern is not.\n\nOh thanks for the heads-up, I always thought that LuaJit is what we should assume as available, with everyone having `runtime = \"LuaJit\"` in their luarc. 😅 \nhttps://github.com/search?type=code&q=path%3Aluarc.json+LuaJIT\n",
